      "body": "## Motivation\r\n\r\nEnable `XiaomiMiMo/MiMo-V2-Flash` & `XiaomiMiMo/MiMo-V2.5` models on Xeon CPUs.\r\n\r\n## Modifications\r\n\r\n- Config dtype conversion: `MiMoV2Config` loads and stores its config items in a Dict rather than normal config object. An on-the-fly conversion is added to align the format.\r\n- Loosen RoPE Q/K Headnum check: MiMo-V2.5 uses grouped-query attention in the vision tower, the inference was blocked by a over-strict Q/K head_num check in `rope.cpp`.\r\n- Adaptive device orientation: In `mimo_audio.py` this was hard-coded as CUDA device.\r\n- Fix for `req_to_token` index overflow: `req_pool_id` was stored as an int32, models that support long context input like `XiaomiMiMo/MiMo-V2.5` would cause an overflow for default service launching parameters: (max_context_len = 1,048,580, req_pool_id can reach 2048, 2048 * 1,048,580 = 2,147,491,840 > INT32_MAX). Casting `req_pool_id` to int64_t to avoid this. (was covered in #44665 )\r\n\r\n## Accuracy Tests\r\n\r\nService launching commands:\r\n\r\n```\r\nsglang serve --model-path XiaomiMiMo/MiMo-V2-Flash --device cpu --trust-remote-code --disable-overlap-schedule --tp 4 --reasoning-parser mimo --tool-call-parser mimo --host 0.0.0.0 --port 30000\r\n\r\nsglang serve --model-path XiaomiMiMo/MiMo-V2.5 --device cpu --trust-remote-code --disable-overlap-schedule --tp 4 --reasoning-parser mimo --tool-call-parser mimo --host 0.0.0.0 --port 30000\r\n```\r\n\r\nTested with [example request](https://docs.sglang.io/cookbook/autoregressive/Xiaomi/MiMo-V2.5#4-2-reasoning-output), output makes sense (pasting MiMo-V2.5 output as example):\r\n\r\n```\r\n====== Reasoning ======\r\n9.11 vs 9.9\r\n\r\nLet me compare these two decimal numbers carefully.\r\n\r\n9.9 = 9.90\r\n9.11 = 9.11\r\n\r\n9.90 > 9.11\r\n\r\nSo 9.9 is larger.\r\n====== Answer ======\r\n## Comparing 9.11 and 9.9\r\n\r\nTo compare these properly, I'll align the decimal places:\r\n\r\n- **9.11** = 9.11\r\n- **9.90** = 9.90\r\n\r\nLooking at the tenths place: **9 > 1**\r\n\r\n**9.9 is larger.**\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Checklist\r\n\r\n- [ ] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\r\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\r\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\r\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\r\n- [ ] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\r\n\r\n## Review and Merge Process\r\n\r\n1. Ping Merge Oncalls to start the process. See the [PR Merge Process](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/MAINTAINER.md#pull-request-merge-process).\r\n2. Get approvals from [CODEOWNERS](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/CODEOWNERS) and other reviewers.\r\n3. Trigger CI tests with [comments](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#how-to-trigger-ci-tests) or contact authorized users to do so.\r\n   - Common commands include `/tag-and-rerun-ci`, `/tag-run-ci-label`, `/rerun-failed-ci`\r\n4. After green CI and required approvals, ask Merge Oncalls or people with Write permission to merge the PR.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\r\n---\r\n### CI States\r\n\r\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:white_check_mark: [Run #40623138149](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40623138149)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\r\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40623138103](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40623138103)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\r\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #40623138084](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40623138084)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\r\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
